      "created_at": "2015-01-06T19:24:14.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p><span>I was playing The Sentinels against The Dreamer when Projected Paralysis came out. &nbsp;Since that card targets </span><span>\"The player with the most cards in play\"&nbsp;</span><span>we had to stop the game for a bit to figure out which of The Sentinels cards count toward cards in play. &nbsp;</span></p><p><span>Ignoring things like ongoings, Is it:</span></p><p><span>The \"Sentinels\" team card + All&nbsp;</span><span>four hero cards?</span></p><p><span>The \"Sentinels\" team card + only the active hero&nbsp;</span><span>cards?</span></p><p><span>All four hero cards?</span></p><p><span>Only the active hero cards?</span></p><p>We decided that all four hero cards counted towards cards in play, regardless of whether they were active or incapped, but that the team card didn't. &nbsp;Was that correct or should we have done that differently.</p><p>[I tried to search the forum for a ruling on this, but it's hard to use Sentinels as a search term.]</p>",
